<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Layer on Typophile Archive</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/layer/</link><description>Recent content in Layer on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 07 May 2013 20:33:00 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/tags/layer/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Slab Happy - a layered typographic system</title><link>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/102847/</link><pubDate>Tue, 07 May 2013 20:33:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>https://jolg42.github.io/typophile/102847/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Inspired by neutral slab serifs with an added twist, Slab Happy is a typographic system consisting of eight layerable fonts with infinite combinations. Slab Happy looks best when set in display sizes, but functions just as well at smaller point sizes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The complete Slab Happy family consists of: Regular, Bold, Outline, 3D, Stitches, Fill, Shadow, and Crosshatch.&lt;/p&gt;
